    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow"
          >⬡ Salesforce · <span data-lang="pt">Lição 2 · dados</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Lesson 2 · data</span></span
        >
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">SOQL: SQL com <strong>um objeto raiz</strong></span
          ><span data-lang="en">SOQL: SQL with <strong>one root object</strong></span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >A anatomia de uma query, as 6 diferenças que pegam quem vem do
            SQL, relacionamentos sem JOIN — e <strong>9 exercícios de
            escrita</strong> espalhados pela lição para o conhecimento
            grudar. Escreva sem copiar; o sandbox corrige na hora.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >A query's anatomy, the 6 differences that trip up SQL folks,
            relationships without JOIN — and <strong>9 writing
            exercises</strong> spread through the lesson so the knowledge
            sticks. Write without copying; the sandbox corrects you
            instantly.</span
          >
        </p>
      </header>

      <nav class="concept-nav">
        <a href="0001-apex-basics.html">Apex</a
        ><a href="0002-soql-basics.html">SOQL →</a
        ><a href="../../../index.html">Hub</a>
      </nav>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">O modelo mental: SQL de leitura, um objeto raiz</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The mental model: read-only SQL, one root object</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >SOQL (<strong>Salesforce Object Query Language</strong>) é a
          linguagem de consulta da plataforma. O vocabulário traduz direto do
          SQL: tabela vira <strong>objeto</strong> (<code>Account</code>,
          <code>Contact</code>), linha vira <strong>registro</strong>, coluna
          vira <strong>campo</strong>. Mas o design é diferente em tudo que
          importa:</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >SOQL (<strong>Salesforce Object Query Language</strong>) is the
          platform's query language. The vocabulary translates directly from
          SQL: table becomes <strong>object</strong> (<code>Account</code>,
          <code>Contact</code>), row becomes <strong>record</strong>, column
          becomes <strong>field</strong>. But the design differs in everything
          that matters:</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Só lê</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              ><strong>Não existe</strong> INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE em SOQL.
              Escrita é DML do Apex (lição 1).</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >There is <strong>no</strong> INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE in SOQL.
              Writing is Apex DML (lesson 1).</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Um objeto raiz</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >O <code>FROM</code> externo tem <strong>um objeto raiz</strong>.
              Objetos relacionados entram por caminhos, subqueries e
              semi-joins suportados.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >The outer <code>FROM</code> has <strong>one root object</strong>.
              Related objects enter through paths, subqueries, and supported
              semi-joins.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="k">SELECT</span> Name, Industry, AnnualRevenue
<span class="k">FROM</span> Account
<span class="k">WHERE</span> Industry = <span class="s">'Technology'</span>
<span class="k">ORDER BY</span> AnnualRevenue <span class="k">DESC</span>
<span class="k">LIMIT</span> 10</code></pre>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Os operadores de filtro são os amigos de sempre — mais alguns
          exemplos de cada:</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >The filter operators are the usual friends — a few examples of
          each:</span
        >
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="k">WHERE</span> Industry != <span class="s">'Technology'</span>
<span class="k">WHERE</span> Industry <span class="k">IN</span> (<span class="s">'Technology'</span>, <span class="s">'Consulting'</span>)
<span class="k">WHERE</span> Name <span class="k">LIKE</span> <span class="s">'A%'</span>
<span class="k">WHERE</span> AnnualRevenue &gt; 1000000
<span class="k">WHERE</span> CreatedDate = <span class="k">TODAY</span>
<span class="k">WHERE</span> Industry = <span class="k">NULL</span></code></pre>
      <p class="kicker">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><code>%</code> é curinga; datas aceitam literais como
          <code>TODAY</code> e <code>LAST_N_DAYS:n</code>; campo vazio usa
          <code>= null</code>, não <code>IS NULL</code>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><code>%</code> is a wildcard; dates accept literals such as
          <code>TODAY</code> and <code>LAST_N_DAYS:n</code>; an empty field uses
          <code>= null</code>, not <code>IS NULL</code>.</span
        >
      </p>
      <p class="cite">
        <span data-lang="pt">Fontes:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Sources:</span>
        <a href="https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/database_basics_dotnet/sql_to_soql"
          >Trailhead — Move from SQL to SOQL</a
        >
        ·
        <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/sfdc-api/guide/sforce_api_calls_soql.html"
          >SOQL Reference</a
        >
      </p>

      <div class="playground sql-sandbox" data-sql-sandbox data-key="sf-soql-basic">
