          ><span data-lang="en">Your SOQL query</span></label
        >
        <textarea
          id="sql-editor-1"
          spellcheck="false"
          autocapitalize="off"
          autocomplete="off"
          placeholder="SELECT ..."
        ></textarea>
        <div class="sandbox-actions">
          <button class="primary" type="button" data-check-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Executar ⌘↵</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Run ⌘↵</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-hint-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Pista</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Hint</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-solution-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Mostrar solução</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Show solution</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-next-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Próxima →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Next →</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="sandbox-feedback" data-feedback aria-live="polite"></div>
        <script type="application/json" data-questions>
          [
            {
              "id": "basic-select",
              "ptTitle": "1 · Escolha campos",
              "enTitle": "1 · Choose fields",
              "ptPrompt": "Mostre Name e Industry de todas as contas.",
              "enPrompt": "Show Name and Industry for every account.",
              "schema": ["Account(Id, Name, Industry, AnnualRevenue, Phone)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT Name, Industry FROM Account"],
              "ptHint": "SELECT com dois campos, FROM Account. Não use SELECT * — não existe.",
              "enHint": "SELECT with two fields, FROM Account. Don't use SELECT * — it doesn't exist."
            },
            {
              "id": "basic-where",
              "ptTitle": "2 · Filtre linhas",
              "enTitle": "2 · Filter rows",
              "ptPrompt": "Mostre Name das contas da indústria Technology.",
              "enPrompt": "Show Name of accounts in the Technology industry.",
              "schema": ["Account(Id, Name, Industry, AnnualRevenue, Phone)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT Name FROM Account WHERE Industry = 'Technology'"],
              "ptHint": "Adicione WHERE Industry = 'Technology' depois do FROM.",
              "enHint": "Add WHERE Industry = 'Technology' after FROM."
            },
            {
              "id": "basic-order-limit",
              "ptTitle": "3 · Ordene e limite",
              "enTitle": "3 · Order and limit",
              "ptPrompt": "As 5 contas com maior AnnualRevenue: mostre Name e AnnualRevenue.",
              "enPrompt": "The 5 accounts with the highest AnnualRevenue: show Name and AnnualRevenue.",
              "schema": ["Account(Id, Name, Industry, AnnualRevenue, Phone)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT Name, AnnualRevenue FROM Account ORDER BY AnnualRevenue DESC LIMIT 5"],
              "ptHint": "ORDER BY AnnualRevenue DESC e depois LIMIT 5 — nessa ordem.",
              "enHint": "ORDER BY AnnualRevenue DESC then LIMIT 5 — in that order."
            },
            {
              "id": "basic-in-like",
              "ptTitle": "4 · Combine filtros",
              "enTitle": "4 · Combine filters",
              "ptPrompt": "Contas de Technology OU Consulting cujo nome começa com A: mostre Name.",
              "enPrompt": "Accounts in Technology OR Consulting whose name starts with A: show Name.",
              "schema": ["Account(Id, Name, Industry, AnnualRevenue, Phone)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT Name FROM Account WHERE Industry IN ('Technology','Consulting') AND Name LIKE 'A%'"],
              "ptHint": "IN para a lista de indústrias, LIKE 'A%' para o curinga, AND junta os dois.",
              "enHint": "IN for the industry list, LIKE 'A%' for the wildcard, AND joins both."
            }
          ]
        </script>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">As 6 diferenças que pegam quem vem do SQL</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The 6 differences that trip up SQL folks</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>1 · Sem <code>SELECT *</code></h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Liste os campos. <code>FIELDS(ALL)</code> existe em contextos
              suportados, mas consultas não limitadas precisam ser
              <strong>bounded</strong> a no máximo 200 linhas — normalmente
              com <code>LIMIT 200</code> ou menor (listas de até 200 IDs também
              podem limitar). Em Apex, prefira a lista explícita.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >List the fields. <code>FIELDS(ALL)</code> exists in supported
              contexts, but unbounded queries must be <strong>bounded</strong>
              to at most 200 rows—usually with <code>LIMIT 200</code> or less
              (lists of up to 200 IDs can also provide the bound). In Apex,
              prefer an explicit field list.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>2 · Sem <code>JOIN</code> arbitrário</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >SOQL não tem a cláusula JOIN livre do SQL. Use relacionamentos
              declarados: ponto, subquery e semi-/anti-join com
              <code>IN</code>/<code>NOT IN</code>.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >SOQL has no arbitrary SQL JOIN clause. Use declared
              relationships: dot notation, subqueries, and semi-/anti-joins
              with <code>IN</code>/<code>NOT IN</code>.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>3 · <code>=</code> ignora maiúsculas</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              ><code>WHERE Name = 'acme'</code> encontra <code>Acme</code> e
              <code>ACME</code>. Campos de texto comuns ignoram case; campos
              únicos configurados como case-sensitive são a exceção.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              ><code>WHERE Name = 'acme'</code> matches <code>Acme</code> and
              <code>ACME</code>. Ordinary text fields ignore case; unique
              fields configured as case-sensitive are the exception.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>4 · <code>OFFSET</code> ≤ 2000</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              ><code>OFFSET</code> pula no máximo 2000 linhas. <code>LIMIT</code>
              não é obrigatório, mas paginação normalmente combina
              <code>ORDER BY</code>, <code>LIMIT</code> e
              <code>OFFSET</code>.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              ><code>OFFSET</code> skips at most 2,000 rows.
              <code>LIMIT</code> isn't required, but pagination normally
              combines <code>ORDER BY</code>, <code>LIMIT</code>, and
              <code>OFFSET</code>.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>5 · Sem <code>UNION</code></h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >SOQL não combina result sets com <code>UNION</code>. Faça
              consultas separadas e, quando necessário, una resultados
              compatíveis no Apex.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >SOQL doesn't combine result sets with <code>UNION</code>. Run
              separate queries and, when needed, merge compatible results in
              Apex.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>6 · Sufixos <code>__c</code> / <code>__r</code></h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Objetos e campos customizados: <code>Book__c</code>; o
              relacionamento customizado usa <code>__r</code>.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Custom objects and fields: <code>Book__c</code>; the custom
              relationship uses <code>__r</code>.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Relacionamento sem JOIN: ponto e subquery</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Relationship without JOIN: dot and subquery</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Todo campo de lookup é uma <strong>relação filho → pai</strong>:
          um <code>Contact</code> tem um <code>Account</code>. Para subir a
          hierarquia, use <strong>notação de ponto</strong>:</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Every lookup field is a <strong>child → parent</strong> relation: a
          <code>Contact</code> has one <code>Account</code>. To go up the
          hierarchy, use <strong>dot notation</strong>:</span
        >
      </p>
      <p class="kicker">
        <span data-lang="pt">Filho → pai: ponto (até 5 níveis acima)</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Child → parent: dot (up to 5 levels up)</span>
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="k">SELECT</span> LastName, Account.Name, Account.Industry
<span class="k">FROM</span> Contact
<span class="k">WHERE</span> Account.Industry = <span class="s">'Technology'</span></code></pre>
      <p class="kicker">
        <span data-lang="pt">Pai → filhos: subquery com o nome do relacionamento</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Parent → children: subquery with the relationship name</span>
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="k">SELECT</span> Name, (<span class="k">SELECT</span> LastName <span class="k">FROM</span> Contacts)
<span class="k">FROM</span> Account</code></pre>
      <p class="kicker">
        <span data-lang="pt">Custom: Book__c aponta para Author__c via Author__r</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Custom: Book__c looks up to Author__c via Author__r</span>
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="k">SELECT</span> Title__c, Author__r.Name <span class="k">FROM</span> Book__c</code></pre>
      <div class="callout key">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >No SOQL com <code>FROM Contact</code>, ponto sobe como
          <code>Account.Name</code>; depois da query, o Apex lê
          <code>contact.Account?.Name</code>. Subquery desce com
          <code>SELECT … FROM Contacts</code>. Nomes padrão costumam ser o
          plural; sempre confirme, especialmente nos relacionamentos custom.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >In SOQL with <code>FROM Contact</code>, dots go up as
          <code>Account.Name</code>; after the query, Apex reads
          <code>contact.Account?.Name</code>. A subquery goes down with
          <code>SELECT … FROM Contacts</code>. Standard names are often the
          plural; always verify, especially for custom relationships.</span
        >
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        <span data-lang="pt">Fontes:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Sources:</span>
        <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/blogs/2013/05/basic-soql-relationship-queries"
          >Salesforce — Basic SOQL Relationship Queries</a
        >
        ·
        <a href="https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/soql-for-admins/create-relationship-queries-with-standard-objects"
          >Trailhead — Relationship Queries</a
        >
      </p>

      <div class="playground sql-sandbox" data-sql-sandbox data-key="sf-soql-rel">
        <div class="sandbox-head">
          <div>
            <h3 data-question-title></h3>
            <p data-question-prompt></p>
          </div>
          <span class="sandbox-count" data-count></span>
        </div>
        <div class="sandbox-schema" data-schema></div>
        <label for="sql-editor-2"
          ><span data-lang="pt">Sua consulta SOQL</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Your SOQL query</span></label
        >
        <textarea
          id="sql-editor-2"
          spellcheck="false"
          autocapitalize="off"
          autocomplete="off"
          placeholder="SELECT ..."
        ></textarea>
        <div class="sandbox-actions">
          <button class="primary" type="button" data-check-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Executar ⌘↵</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Run ⌘↵</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-hint-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Pista</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Hint</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-solution-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Mostrar solução</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Show solution</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-next-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Próxima →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Next →</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="sandbox-feedback" data-feedback aria-live="polite"></div>
        <script type="application/json" data-questions>
          [
            {
              "id": "rel-dot-up",
              "ptTitle": "1 · Suba para o pai",
              "enTitle": "1 · Go up to the parent",
              "ptPrompt": "LastName e nome da conta de cada contato — só de contas da indústria Technology.",
              "enPrompt": "Each contact's LastName and their account's name — only for Technology accounts.",
              "schema": ["Contact(Id, LastName, Email, AccountId)", "Account(Id, Name, Industry)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT LastName, Account.Name FROM Contact WHERE Account.Industry = 'Technology'"],
              "ptHint": "No SELECT, suba com Account.Name (ponto). No WHERE, o mesmo: Account.Industry = 'Technology'.",
              "enHint": "In SELECT, go up with Account.Name (dot). In WHERE, same thing: Account.Industry = 'Technology'."
            },
            {
              "id": "rel-subquery",
              "ptTitle": "2 · Desça para os filhos",
              "enTitle": "2 · Go down to the children",
              "ptPrompt": "Nome de cada conta junto com os LastName dos seus contatos.",
              "enPrompt": "Each account's name together with its contacts' LastName.",
              "schema": ["Contact(Id, LastName, Email, AccountId)", "Account(Id, Name, Industry)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT Name, (SELECT LastName FROM Contacts) FROM Account"],
              "ptHint": "O FROM principal é Account; a subquery vai entre parênteses dentro do SELECT: (SELECT LastName FROM Contacts).",
              "enHint": "The main FROM is Account; the subquery goes in parentheses inside SELECT: (SELECT LastName FROM Contacts)."
            },
            {
              "id": "rel-custom",
              "ptTitle": "3 · Objeto custom",
              "enTitle": "3 · Custom object",
              "ptPrompt": "Title__c de cada livro com o nome do autor.",
              "enPrompt": "Each book's Title__c with the author's name.",
              "schema": ["Book__c(Id, Title__c, Author__c)", "Author__c(Id, Name)", "lookup Book__c.Author__c → Author__c (relationship: Author__r)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT Title__c, Author__r.Name FROM Book__c"],
              "ptHint": "O campo lookup Author__c vira Author__r na navegação: Author__r.Name sobe até o nome.",
              "enHint": "The lookup field Author__c becomes Author__r when navigating: Author__r.Name goes up to the name."
            }
          ]
        </script>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Agregação: <code>GROUP BY</code> devolve <code>AggregateResult</code></span
        ><span data-lang="en">Aggregation: <code>GROUP BY</code> returns <code>AggregateResult</code></span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><code>COUNT()</code>, <code>SUM()</code>, <code>AVG()</code>,
          <code>MIN()</code>, <code>MAX()</code> funcionam como no SQL, com
          <code>GROUP BY</code> e <code>HAVING</code>. Queries agrupadas
          retornam linhas <strong>AggregateResult</strong>, lidas com
          <code>get()</code>; um <code>COUNT()</code> isolado pode ser
          atribuído diretamente a um <code>Integer</code>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><code>COUNT()</code>, <code>SUM()</code>, <code>AVG()</code>,
          <code>MIN()</code>, <code>MAX()</code> work like SQL, with
          <code>GROUP BY</code> and <code>HAVING</code>. Grouped queries return
          <strong>AggregateResult</strong> rows read with <code>get()</code>;
          a bare <code>COUNT()</code> can be assigned directly to an
          <code>Integer</code>.</span
        >
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span data-lang="pt"><span class="c">// quem tem mais de 5 contatos?</span></span
><span data-lang="en"><span class="c">// who has more than 5 contacts?</span></span>
List&lt;AggregateResult&gt; results = [
    <span class="k">SELECT</span> AccountId, <span class="k">COUNT</span>(Id) cnt
    <span class="k">FROM</span> Contact
    <span class="k">GROUP BY</span> AccountId
    <span class="k">HAVING</span> <span class="k">COUNT</span>(Id) &gt; 5
];
<span class="k">for</span> (AggregateResult ar : results) {
    System.debug(ar.<span class="k">get</span>(<span class="s">'AccountId'</span>) + <span class="s">' → '</span> + ar.<span class="k">get</span>(<span class="s">'cnt'</span>));
}</code></pre>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >E dentro do Apex, a query mora <strong>entre colchetes</strong> —
          variáveis locais entram com <code>:</code> (bind variable):</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >And inside Apex, the query lives <strong>between brackets</strong>
          — local variables enter with <code>:</code> (bind variable):</span
        >
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code>String industry = <span class="s">'Technology'</span>;
List&lt;Account&gt; accs = [<span class="k">SELECT</span> Name <span class="k">FROM</span> Account <span class="k">WHERE</span> Industry = :industry];</code></pre>

      <div class="playground sql-sandbox" data-sql-sandbox data-key="sf-soql-agg">
        <div class="sandbox-head">
          <div>
            <h3 data-question-title></h3>
            <p data-question-prompt></p>
          </div>
          <span class="sandbox-count" data-count></span>
        </div>
        <div class="sandbox-schema" data-schema></div>
        <label for="sql-editor-3"
          ><span data-lang="pt">Sua consulta SOQL</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Your SOQL query</span></label
        >
        <textarea
          id="sql-editor-3"
          spellcheck="false"
          autocapitalize="off"
          autocomplete="off"
          placeholder="SELECT ..."
        ></textarea>
        <div class="sandbox-actions">
          <button class="primary" type="button" data-check-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Executar ⌘↵</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Run ⌘↵</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-hint-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Pista</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Hint</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-solution-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Mostrar solução</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Show solution</span></button
          ><button type="button" data-next-sql>
            <span data-lang="pt">Próxima →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Next →</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="sandbox-feedback" data-feedback aria-live="polite"></div>
        <script type="application/json" data-questions>
          [
            {
              "id": "agg-count",
              "ptTitle": "1 · Conte por grupo",
              "enTitle": "1 · Count per group",
              "ptPrompt": "Quantas contas existem por indústria: Industry e a quantidade.",
              "enPrompt": "How many accounts exist per industry: Industry and the count.",
              "schema": ["Account(Id, Name, Industry, AnnualRevenue, Phone)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT Industry, COUNT(Id) FROM Account GROUP BY Industry"],
              "ptHint": "SELECT Industry, COUNT(Id) … GROUP BY Industry — o campo do SELECT vira o grupo.",
              "enHint": "SELECT Industry, COUNT(Id) … GROUP BY Industry — the selected field becomes the group."
            },
            {
              "id": "agg-having",
              "ptTitle": "2 · Filtre grupos",
              "enTitle": "2 · Filter groups",
              "ptPrompt": "Os AccountId que têm mais de 5 contatos: AccountId e a quantidade.",
              "enPrompt": "The AccountIds that have more than 5 contacts: AccountId and the count.",
              "schema": ["Contact(Id, LastName, Email, AccountId)"],
              "answers": ["SELECT AccountId, COUNT(Id) FROM Contact GROUP BY AccountId HAVING COUNT(Id) > 5"],
              "ptHint": "WHERE filtra LINHAS, HAVING filtra GRUPOS. Depois do GROUP BY, use HAVING COUNT(Id) > 5.",
              "enHint": "WHERE filters ROWS, HAVING filters GROUPS. After GROUP BY, use HAVING COUNT(Id) > 5."
            }
          ]
        </script>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">5</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Checagem rápida</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Quick check</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="mcq" data-mcq>
        <p class="mcq-q">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Você quer, numa query só, cada conta e seus contatos. O que
            usar?</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >You want, in one query, each account and its contacts. What do
            you use?</span
          >
        </p>
        <div class="mcq-opts">
          <button
            class="mcq-opt"
            data-correct="true"
            data-fb-pt="Exato: subquery pai → filho: SELECT Name, (SELECT LastName FROM Contacts) FROM Account. Contas e contatos numa resposta só, sem JOIN."
            data-fb-en="Exactly: parent → child subquery: SELECT Name, (SELECT LastName FROM Contacts) FROM Account. Accounts and contacts in one result, no JOIN."
          >
            <span data-lang="pt">Subquery dentro do SELECT</span
            ><span data-lang="en">A subquery inside SELECT</span>
          </button>
          <button
            class="mcq-opt"
            data-correct="false"
            data-fb-pt="Não existe JOIN em SOQL. A junção de tabelas do SQL vira navegação de relacionamento: ponto para subir, subquery para descer."
            data-fb-en="There is no JOIN in SOQL. SQL's table joining becomes relationship navigation: dot to go up, subquery to go down."
          >
            <span data-lang="pt">Um JOIN com Accounts</span
            ><span data-lang="en">A JOIN with Accounts</span>
          </button>
          <button
            class="mcq-opt"
            data-correct="false"
            data-fb-pt="O FROM externo tem um objeto raiz — não dá para listar Account e Contact como raízes lado a lado. Para descer de Account até Contacts, use a subquery."
            data-fb-en="The outer FROM has one root object — you can't list Account and Contact as side-by-side roots. To go down from Account to Contacts, use the subquery."
          >
            <span data-lang="pt">FROM Account, Contact</span
            ><span data-lang="en">FROM Account, Contact</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="mcq-fb" data-fb></div>
      </div>

      <div class="mcq" data-mcq>
        <p class="mcq-q">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >O que acontece com <code>SELECT Name FROM Account WHERE Name =
            'acme'</code> quando o registro gravado é <code>Acme</code>?</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >What happens with <code>SELECT Name FROM Account WHERE Name =
            'acme'</code> when the stored record is <code>Acme</code>?</span
          >
        </p>
        <div class="mcq-opts">
          <button
            class="mcq-opt"
            data-correct="true"
            data-fb-pt="Correto: Account.Name é um campo de texto comum, então 'acme' encontra Acme e ACME. Campos únicos case-sensitive são a exceção."
            data-fb-en="Correct: Account.Name is an ordinary text field, so 'acme' matches Acme and ACME. Case-sensitive unique fields are the exception."
          >
            <span data-lang="pt">Encontra — ignora maiúsculas</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Finds it — case is ignored</span>
          </button>
          <button
            class="mcq-opt"
            data-correct="false"
            data-fb-pt="Para Account.Name, = ignora maiúsculas. SOQL não tem um comparador case-sensitive universal; a exceção são campos únicos configurados como case-sensitive."
            data-fb-en="For Account.Name, = ignores case. SOQL has no universal case-sensitive comparator; the exception is unique fields configured as case-sensitive."
          >
            <span data-lang="pt">Retorna zero registros</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Returns zero records</span>
          </button>
          <button
            class="mcq-opt"
            data-correct="false"
            data-fb-pt="SOQL não reescreve nem normaliza seus dados — ele apenas compara sem diferenciar maiúsculas de minúsculas. O dado gravado continua 'Acme'."
            data-fb-en="SOQL neither rewrites nor normalizes your data — it just compares without distinguishing upper from lower case. The stored data stays 'Acme'."
          >
            <span data-lang="pt">Erro de sintaxe na query</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Query syntax error</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="mcq-fb" data-fb></div>
      </div>

